    "category": "",
    "tagline": "Throttle requests per client to protect your API from abuse and overload.",
    "keywords": "The built-in Microsoft.AspNetCore.RateLimiting middleware (.NET 7+) provides four algorithms out of the box. Fixed window allows N requests per time window (e.g. 100 per minute). Sliding window is smoother — it divides the window into segments so bursts are spread out. Token bucket allows bursts up to a bucket size, then refills at a steady rate. Concurrency limits simultaneous in-flight requests. Rate limiters can be global, per-named-policy (applied via attribute or endpoint metadata), or per-partition — meaning you can limit per IP address, per user, or per API key, each with its own independent counter. UseRateLimiter() must be placed after UseRouting() Fixed window: simplest — N requests per period; vulnerable to boundary bursts Sliding window: smoother — spreads requests across sub-w"
